    "carry_forward": [
      "A final-verification receipt reading FAILED is not evidence the science failed. Grep its log for FAILED|ERROR and check whether a pytest summary line exists before re-opening an issue or re-litigating physics: here the FAILED receipt's log held zero failures, stopped at 70% of 123 tests, and the same suite passed 120/3-skipped on either side of it.",
      "A passing final-verification receipt is bound to the closeout record's review_signature, so any later edit to subagents, agent_continuity, scope_decisions, maintenance or map_delta voids it. final_verification.py check prints that signature in seconds; compare it against the receipt before trusting a prior PASS or paying for another full suite, which cost 10:55 here.",
      "Do not read closed_issues.md as evidence that an iteration actually closed. The gate requires the entry to be there before it will validate the closeout, so a resolved-looking entry can precede its passing receipt by hours; 1DMIX-057's preceded it by 3h10m. Check loop_state for an accepted closed_at before reporting an issue as closed."
    ],
